<div .jumbotron .text-center>
    <div .container>
        <div .row>
            <h1 .header>
                #{appName}
            <h2>
                a blogging platform for mathematicians
                
            $maybe uid <- maybeUserId
                <a href=@{UserHomeR uid} .btn.btn-primary.btn-lg>
                    My Homepage
            $nothing
                <a href=@{AuthR LoginR} .btn.btn-primary.btn-lg>
                    Sign up / Sign in
                <a href=@{EntriesR} .btn.btn-default.btn-lg>
                    Explore Posts

<div .container>
    <div .bs-docs-section>
        <h2>What Is Functor Network?</h2>
            <p>Functor Network is a ready-to-use blogging platform built specifically for mathematicians.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><p><strong>Ready to Use:</strong> No software to install, no servers to maintain, and no configuration files to manage. Simply sign up and start writing on a fully managed platform.</p></li>
                <li><p><strong>Blog:</strong> Express your ideas, share in-depth insights, and build a personal space to document your mathematical journey.</p></li>
                <li><p><strong>Mathematician:</strong> The term <em>mathematician</em> here is in a broad sense, including people studying math at any level as well as professionals in related fields. While we offer special support for mathematicians, anyone can register a blog site on our platform and express themselves on a variety of topics, whether they’re related to math or not.</p></li>
                <li><p><strong>Network:</strong> Write as part of an interconnected community rather than in isolation. Connect with other writers, reach new audiences, and discover related mathematical topics across the network.</p></li>
    
    <hr>
    <div .bs-docs-section>
        <h2>Key Feature</h2>
        <p>To the best of our knowledge, Functor Network is the only blogging platform built around a full <strong>TeX Live distribution</strong>, bringing the full power of LaTeX to your writing. This enables you to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><p><strong>Use LaTeX Packages:</strong> Import your favorite LaTeX packages without being limited to a small, predefined subset.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Define Custom Commands:</strong> Create your own macros to suit your workflow and reuse them throughout your posts.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Write with Theorem Environments:</strong> Structure your theorems, lemmas, and proofs using LaTeX theorem environments.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Cross-Reference with Ease:</strong> Reference equations, theorems, bibliographic citations, and other elements throughout your posts.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Reuse Existing TeX Documents:</strong> Bring your existing <code>.tex</code> source files into your blog posts with minimal, if any, modifications.</p></li>
        
    <hr>
    <div .bs-docs-section>
        <h2>More Features</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><p><strong>One-Click PDF Export:</strong> Readers who prefer reading on paper can export any blog post as a PDF with a single click.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Lean Syntax Highlighting:</strong> In addition to syntax highlighting for common programming languages, we also support syntax highlighting for the Lean theorem prover.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Style-Decoupled Editing:</strong> Focus on your content while writing; presentation and styling are handled separately.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Math-Aware Dark Mode:</strong> Mathematical symbols automatically adapt to the active theme, ensuring optimal clarity and readability in both light and dark modes.</p></li>
            <li><p><strong>Minimalist by Design:</strong> No clutter. No distractions. Just a clean, efficient, and secure space for your thoughts.</p></li>
        